-1}"] ["math" "{y}^{-2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337619" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{6y+1}{2{y}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337619" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337619" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{-2}{e}^{1/(2y)}"] ["math" "{y}^{-3}{e}^{-1/(2y)}"] ["math" "{y}^{-3}{e}^{1/(2y)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337619" "field" "field-6" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{-3}{e}^{1/(2y)}"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337619" "field" "field-7" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337619" "field" "field-7" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{-2}{e}^{1/(2y)}\\cdot (2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-xy\\,\\text{d}y)=0"] ["math" "{y}^{-3}{e}^{-1/(2y)}\\cdot (2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-xy\\,\\text{d}y)=0"] ["math" "{y}^{-3}{e}^{1/(2y)}\\cdot (2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-xy\\,\\text{d}y)=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337619" "field" "field-7" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{-3}{e}^{1/(2y)}\\cdot (2{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-xy\\,\\text{d}y)=0"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose we would like to find an integrating factor to convert the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}{y}^{′}=-x{y}^{3}-x,\\,x>0\n$$\n\ninto an exact equation using an integrating factor. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n{{field-1}}=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form. This gives\n\n$$\n{{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nLet's denote\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=x({y}^{3}+1),\\,Q(x,y)={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\,{{field-4}}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\,{{field-5}}\n$$\n\nSince for this equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})={{field-6}},\n$$\n\nwhich depends on $y$ only, then an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)={{field-7}},\n$$\n\nand we arrive at the exact equation\n\n$$\n{{field-8}}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y=0,\n$$\n\nwe have that if\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})=h(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $h(y)$ is independent of $x,$ then an integrating factor for the equation is\n\n$$\nI(y)=\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int h(y)\\,\\text{d}y)\n$$\n\nwhere $\\operatorname{exp}⁡(y)$ denotes the exponential function ${e}^{y}.$\n\nFirst, we rewrite our equation in differential form: \n\n$$\nx({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nLet's denote \n\n$$\nP(x,y)=x({y}^{3}+1),\\,Q(x,y)={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x({y}^{3}+1))=3x{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2})=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}) & =\\frac{1}{x({y}^{3}+1)}(3x{y}^{2}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis a function of $y$ only, we can conclude that an integrating factor for our equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(y) & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{exp}⁡(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{3}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand by multiplying our differential equation by the integrating factor, we have\n\n$$\nI(y)\\cdot (x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=I(y)\\cdot 0\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{{y}^{3}+1}(x({y}^{3}+1)\\,\\text{d}x+{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y)=0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "64e27fff88cb729c782b2da64f3aa25f52937c98305c0cd7f9d19d2a6e4597ea"} {"question" "q-337707" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337707" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{Q}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337707" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{P}(\\frac{∂P}{∂y}-\\frac{∂Q}{∂x})"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14061603/state.json" "file_sha256" "d7b900863b000acb74914637309952b4bb3e7b99973b8d5caa337c0a75eefa40"} {"question" "q-337707" "fiel